WEBVTT

00:01.701 --> 00:05.569
After the kid goes back to his mother's,
you wanna go out and grab some dinner?

00:05.805 --> 00:07.432
I can't go out to dinner, Charlie.

00:07.607 --> 00:08.938
Why not? You got a date?

00:09.109 --> 00:12.806
He said knowing the answer,
but asking anyway just to be polite.

00:13.413 --> 00:14.437
I don't have a date.

00:14.614 --> 00:18.345
He replied, all the while thinking,
"Bite me, you booze-addled buffoon. "

00:19.919 --> 00:21.011
So why can't you go?

00:21.387 --> 00:24.356
Are you kidding?
I'm paying alimony to two women.

00:24.524 --> 00:26.958
I don't have money for luxuries
like eating out.

00:27.127 --> 00:29.288
Or eating in, really.

00:29.462 --> 00:32.090
I'm trying to learn to chew my own cud.

00:32.398 --> 00:35.731
- That's all right. I'll treat.
- No, you've done too much for me already.

00:35.902 --> 00:39.599
Yeah, but it's not like
I'm keeping a tab, $26,382.

00:41.474 --> 00:43.374
To date.

00:43.543 --> 00:46.671
Exactly. So I need to start carrying
my own weight.

00:46.846 --> 00:50.475
Which is actually getting easier
now that I'm wasting away.

00:50.750 --> 00:53.878
- Stop feeling sorry for yourself.
- I'm not feeling sorry for myself.

00:54.053 --> 00:59.491
I'll find something here to eat.
Maybe some scrambled eggs and a Popsicle.

00:59.659 --> 01:02.093
Fine. See you later.

01:09.335 --> 01:12.532
All right, I'm only gonna ask you
one more time.

01:12.705 --> 01:15.333
- Would you like to have dinner with me?
- That depends.

01:15.508 --> 01:18.068
- Where are we going?
- Oh, for God's sake.

01:18.244 --> 01:19.734
What? I don't even get a vote?

01:19.913 --> 01:21.904
You don't get a vote,
you get a free meal.

01:22.081 --> 01:25.710
Well, if I was one of your dates,
you'd ask where I wanted to go.

01:27.187 --> 01:28.620
You're right.

01:30.490 --> 01:32.924
So where do you wanna go, baby?

01:33.526 --> 01:34.550
That's very funny.

01:34.727 --> 01:39.755
No, no, no, let's get something hot in you
and then get something hot in you.

01:39.933 --> 01:41.730
Knock it off.

01:41.901 --> 01:42.925
Gee, you smell good.

01:43.102 --> 01:45.969
You know what? Okay, I'll just stay here
and have a Popsicle.

01:46.139 --> 01:47.766
Oh, you'll be getting the Popsicle.

01:47.941 --> 01:50.341
Fine, fine, fine.
Okay, you pick the restaurant.

01:50.510 --> 01:52.000
Thank you. How about sushi?

01:52.178 --> 01:54.043
Ugh. Not a big fan.

01:56.049 --> 01:58.108
Oh, that's Judith. Keep thinking.

02:01.654 --> 02:04.020
Jake, your mother's here.

02:05.792 --> 02:08.420
Hey, that Popsicle almost...

02:19.005 --> 02:21.337
- Hello.
- Hi. Yeah, he'll be right out.

02:21.507 --> 02:23.839
Do me a favor and take them both.

02:27.013 --> 02:30.176
- Hey, Mom.
- Hey, honey. Would you, uh, wait in the car?

02:30.350 --> 02:33.148
- Who's in trouble? Me or Dad?
- No one's in trouble.

02:33.319 --> 02:35.116
It's you.

02:36.823 --> 02:38.484
If you're gonna chew my ass off...

02:38.658 --> 02:41.991
...just know I'm planning on having it
for breakfast tomorrow.

02:43.229 --> 02:44.856
No, you didn't do anything, Alan.

02:45.031 --> 02:48.592
I just, uh...
I wanted to let you know that, uh...

02:49.202 --> 02:50.692
Boy, this is awkward. Um...

02:50.870 --> 02:52.895
Remember I was dating
Jake's pediatrician?

02:53.072 --> 02:55.506
Yeah, yeah, Melnick.
Uh, what about him?

02:55.675 --> 02:59.111
Well, we started seeing each other again
and it's gotten serious.

02:59.279 --> 03:01.008
Oh, how serious?

03:01.848 --> 03:04.442
He asked me to marry him
and I said yes.

03:05.718 --> 03:08.152
Oh. Wow.

03:08.321 --> 03:09.618
L...

03:09.789 --> 03:11.882
I don't know what to say. Um...

03:12.058 --> 03:13.548
I guess, congratulations.

03:13.726 --> 03:16.854
Thank you. I just wanted to let you know
before we told Jake.

03:17.030 --> 03:18.793
Sure. Sure. I appreciate it.

03:18.965 --> 03:22.457
It's kind of weird, isn't it?
I mean, we spent so many years together.

03:22.635 --> 03:25.297
It's hard for me to think of you married
to somebody else.

03:25.471 --> 03:27.063
Yeah.

03:30.610 --> 03:32.237
Still, I wish you the best, though.

03:32.412 --> 03:34.812
Oh, I know you do. Thank you.

03:36.482 --> 03:38.916
- Well, bye.
- Bye.

03:48.261 --> 03:50.058
Five, six, seven, eight.

03:50.229 --> 03:51.719
&lt;i>No more alimony&lt;/i>

03:51.898 --> 03:53.388
&lt;i>No more alimony&lt;/i>

03:53.566 --> 03:54.999
&lt;i>No more alimony&lt;/i>

03:55.168 --> 03:57.398
&lt;i>No more alimony&lt;/i>

04:25.832 --> 04:27.891
You know the problem with sushi?

04:28.067 --> 04:30.627
You mean, besides eating it with you?

04:30.803 --> 04:33.499
It's all fleshy and flappy and wet.

04:33.673 --> 04:36.141
Feels unnatural against my tongue.

04:36.309 --> 04:37.799
- Hey, Alan?
- What?

04:37.977 --> 04:40.639
I think I know why your marriages
didn't work out.

04:42.281 --> 04:45.876
Oh, stop it.
Now, speaking of marriages...

04:46.052 --> 04:48.486
...the next time we go out to dinner,
it'll be on me.

04:48.654 --> 04:50.986
Because with Judith
getting married again...

04:51.157 --> 04:53.250
...I'll have...

04:53.426 --> 04:54.825
Five, six, seven, eight.

04:54.994 --> 04:56.655
&lt;i>No more alimony&lt;/i>

04:56.829 --> 04:58.319
&lt;i>No more alimony&lt;/i>

04:58.498 --> 05:00.022
&lt;i>No more alimo...&lt;/i>

05:00.633 --> 05:01.861
Hey, Dad.

05:02.035 --> 05:03.559
What are you doing here?

05:03.736 --> 05:06.000
- And how'd you get in?
- Rose let me in.

05:06.672 --> 05:08.401
Hey, guys.

05:08.574 --> 05:10.064
How was dinner?

05:10.243 --> 05:12.211
Forget dinner. What are you doing here?

05:12.378 --> 05:13.743
Keeping Jake company.

05:14.680 --> 05:17.513
But if you let him in,
you had to have been here before him.

05:17.683 --> 05:19.412
Well, yeah.

05:19.585 --> 05:21.018
But if Jake hadrt shown up...

05:21.187 --> 05:24.554
...I'd be gone by now
and you'd never know I was here.

05:24.724 --> 05:28.182
So, what, you just waltz in and make
yourself at home whenever I'm out?

05:28.361 --> 05:29.419
That's not true.

05:29.595 --> 05:31.688
Sometimes you're upstairs asleep.

05:33.366 --> 05:34.663
Wait, let's go back here.

05:34.834 --> 05:37.268
- Jake, why aren't you at your mother's?
- I ran away.

05:37.437 --> 05:39.769
Sometimes you're in the shower.

05:40.840 --> 05:42.808
Rose, please. Why did you run away?

05:42.975 --> 05:44.465
Because I hate it there.

05:45.111 --> 05:47.204
Is this about the upcoming nuptials?

05:47.380 --> 05:49.780
It's nothing to do with puberty, Dad.

05:51.484 --> 05:53.042
It's about Mom getting married.

05:54.854 --> 05:58.153
- I thought you liked Dr. Melnick.
- That was when they were just dating.

05:58.324 --> 06:01.088
Now he thinks he can tell me what to do.
He's not my father.

06:01.260 --> 06:05.458
- You don't do what I tell you to do.
- Yeah, but Mom doesn't care about that.

06:06.299 --> 06:08.358
Alan, if I could just interrupt for one sec.

06:08.534 --> 06:11.435
How do you keep getting in?
I've changed the locks three times.

06:11.604 --> 06:14.835
Yes.
But you didn't change the locksmith.

06:16.576 --> 06:18.737
I could recommend somebody.

06:20.079 --> 06:21.603
Good night, Rose.

06:21.781 --> 06:24.045
I replace everything I eat.

06:24.217 --> 06:25.912
- Good night.
- You know how I do it?

06:26.085 --> 06:28.519
I keep an exact duplicate fridge
at my house.

06:29.388 --> 06:33.188
- Good night, Rose.
- By the way, we're out of Popsicles.

06:34.360 --> 06:36.954
I'm gonna call your mother.
She's probably worried sick.

06:37.130 --> 06:40.293
She's probably in the hot tub
with Dr. Melnick.

06:41.868 --> 06:44.530
How'd you get here?
You steal a car or something?

06:44.971 --> 06:47.439
How can I steal a car? I'm 12.

06:47.607 --> 06:51.202
You kids these days. No imagination.

06:51.844 --> 06:55.109
- I took the bus.
- In L.A.? At night?

06:55.281 --> 06:57.613
You would've been safer stealing a car.

06:57.783 --> 06:59.808
What's your plan?
Where are you headed?

07:00.253 --> 07:01.345
I'm gonna stay here.

07:02.355 --> 07:04.550
Oh, you can't stay here.

07:05.725 --> 07:08.455
- Why not?
- Because you're running away.

07:08.628 --> 07:11.961
Away, according to the dictionary,
means "not here. "

07:12.632 --> 07:15.465
It's usually preceded
by the words "far, far"...

07:15.635 --> 07:17.830
...or in your case, "go. "

07:19.005 --> 07:21.166
Oh, come on.
Why can't I live with you guys?

07:21.340 --> 07:24.468
Oh, Jake, do you have any idea
how much I have to clean up my act...

07:24.644 --> 07:25.804
...when you're here?

07:26.112 --> 07:27.374
What are you talking about?

07:27.547 --> 07:30.311
I see you drink, gamble,
you have strange girls sleep over.

07:30.483 --> 07:34.385
Uh-huh. Drop in unannounced on
a Wednesday and you'll be scarred for life.

07:35.288 --> 07:37.916
I hope you're proud of yourself.
Your mother's crying.

07:38.090 --> 07:39.284
Good.

07:39.458 --> 07:40.550
Hey.

07:40.826 --> 07:43.386
- Don't be mean to your mother.
- You're mean to your mom.

07:43.563 --> 07:45.224
My mother can take it.

07:45.398 --> 07:46.922
She actually feeds on it.

07:48.501 --> 07:51.595
She wanted me to tell you
that she loves you more than anything...

07:51.771 --> 07:54.035
...she and Dr. Melnick
aren't gonna get married...

07:54.207 --> 07:56.505
...until you've had time to adjust
to the idea.

07:56.876 --> 08:00.175
Then they'll never get married,
because I'm never gonna adjust to it.

08:03.549 --> 08:06.143
- Five, six, seven...
- Shut up.

08:09.689 --> 08:13.250
I am a little surprised at you.
I'd think you'd want your mom to be happy.

08:13.426 --> 08:15.417
Hey, she can be happy all she wants...

08:15.595 --> 08:18.120
...I just don't need some jerk
pretending he's my dad.

08:18.297 --> 08:19.559
Oh, why not?

08:20.032 --> 08:21.932
Because I already have a dad.

08:22.101 --> 08:24.296
And he's already a jerk.

08:25.805 --> 08:27.397
All right, buddy.

08:27.573 --> 08:30.064
I'm gonna have to tell you
something pretty heavy.

08:30.243 --> 08:33.610
But I think it's something
that you're old enough to understand.

08:34.680 --> 08:36.705
You can do better than me.

08:37.783 --> 08:39.375
Way better.

08:40.653 --> 08:42.712
Did you know
that I'm not even a real doctor?

08:42.888 --> 08:44.355
But Dr. Melnick is.

08:44.523 --> 08:46.650
- So what?
- So what? Are you kidding?

08:46.826 --> 08:49.886
He makes more money.
He can buy you better presents than I can.

08:50.062 --> 08:53.998
Don't underestimate the value of having
a prescription pad lying around the house.

08:54.433 --> 08:57.561
- Charlie.
- You know, if someone gets sick.

08:57.737 --> 08:59.170
Or bored.

09:00.006 --> 09:01.473
But I only need one dad.

09:01.641 --> 09:03.074
And you'll only have one dad.

09:03.242 --> 09:06.507
But there's nothing that says
you can't call him "Dad" and me "Alan. "

09:07.146 --> 09:08.943
We'll still know who's who.

09:09.448 --> 09:11.712
I'm getting a little misty.

09:14.420 --> 09:16.684
Forget it. I'm never gonna like him.

09:17.290 --> 09:22.091
May I suggest you try a more,
shall we say, practical approach?

09:25.665 --> 09:28.759
Jake, how much does your mom give you
for allowance?

09:29.635 --> 09:31.466
Ten dollars a week.

09:31.637 --> 09:32.865
Okay.

09:33.606 --> 09:38.543
Uh... I'm gonna write down some
figures here and you tell me to stop...

09:38.711 --> 09:43.307
...when you see a number that makes
you feel a little warmer toward Dr. Melnick.

09:48.287 --> 09:51.085
I was so worried about you,
don't you ever do that again.

09:51.257 --> 09:53.725
- Thanks for bringing him back.
- No problem.

09:53.893 --> 09:57.158
- Isn't there something you wanna say?
- Yeah.

09:58.030 --> 10:00.430
I love you, Dr. Melnick.

10:12.345 --> 10:13.369
Let's get you to bed.

10:13.546 --> 10:16.208
- You've got school in the morning...
- Hang on.

10:17.583 --> 10:19.448
Night, Dad. See you, Alan.

10:21.120 --> 10:22.485
Night, buddy.

10:22.655 --> 10:25.146
Boy, he's really warming up to you.

10:25.324 --> 10:27.656
Yeah. Listen,
have you and Judith ever discussed...

10:27.827 --> 10:29.954
...putting Jake on any sort
of medication?

10:31.497 --> 10:33.488
Why? What do you got?

10:34.166 --> 10:36.464
No, no. We haven't. Why?

10:36.635 --> 10:39.229
One minute he hates me,
the next minute he loves me.

10:39.405 --> 10:41.498
Those kind of mood swings
aren't normal.

10:41.674 --> 10:43.505
Oh, no, no, no, don't worry about that.

10:43.676 --> 10:47.009
That's not an emotional problem.
That's more like, uh...

10:47.179 --> 10:49.409
A kind of, uh...

10:50.316 --> 10:52.341
- Charlie?
- We paid him to like you.

10:53.686 --> 10:56.985
- You what?
- And it cost less than you might think.

10:58.958 --> 11:03.156
But that's a good thing.
A bribable child is a controllable child.

11:03.329 --> 11:06.662
Plus, he's not too bright,
so you can lie to him all you want.

11:06.832 --> 11:07.890
- Charlie.
- Oh, come on.

11:08.067 --> 11:11.833
Until he was 10, I had him convinced
that swizzle sticks were money.

11:15.141 --> 11:17.405
Hey, hey, uh, speaking of swizzle sticks.

11:17.576 --> 11:19.771
Have you guys considered
eloping to vegas?

11:20.246 --> 11:21.838
- No...
- I know what you're thinking.

11:22.014 --> 11:26.246
"Tacky, tacky," but actually, it isn't.
It's classy and very romantic.

11:26.719 --> 11:29.483
Yeah, some of the hotel rooms
have those big mirrored walls.

11:29.655 --> 11:32.886
It's like watching your ass bob up
and down in IMAX.

11:34.860 --> 11:36.225
Oh.

11:36.395 --> 11:38.761
We're gonna put things on hold
for a little while.

11:38.931 --> 11:42.799
- Why? You love Judith, don't you?
- Of course. She's a great woman.

11:42.968 --> 11:44.094
How's the sex?

11:45.471 --> 11:47.132
That's a little personal, isn't it?

11:47.506 --> 11:50.134
Hey, I didn't ask
which way you point her.

11:50.443 --> 11:52.570
I wanna make sure you two kids
are compatible.

11:52.745 --> 11:55.407
Oh, well, there's no problem in that area.

11:55.915 --> 11:57.610
See, Alan? It was you.

12:02.822 --> 12:06.918
That's me. The original
one-pump chump. Ha.

12:07.493 --> 12:08.983
So I hear.

12:10.162 --> 12:13.393
The thing is, I'm just not sure
I'm ready to be a stepfather.

12:13.566 --> 12:15.659
Oh, sure you are. You'll be terrific, right?

12:16.035 --> 12:18.595
As long as there's food,
and money in your wallet...

12:18.771 --> 12:20.898
...you'll own the little peckerhead.

12:21.073 --> 12:24.736
Poor baby was exhausted. He fell asleep
as soon as his head hit the pillow.

12:24.910 --> 12:28.038
- Another plus. Sound sleeper.
- Yeah, nothing wakes that kid up.

12:28.214 --> 12:30.182
I've had some real screamers
at my place.

12:32.585 --> 12:34.519
It's getting late. I'd like to go to bed.

12:34.687 --> 12:37.451
Why don't you do that?
Listen, fatherhood is no big deal.

12:37.623 --> 12:41.320
Truth is, with the Internet and everything,
they practically raise themselves.

12:41.494 --> 12:42.791
Alan.

12:43.496 --> 12:45.794
You go ahead, honey. I'll be in a second.

12:47.600 --> 12:50.933
I don't know. I just think I need
some time to get used to the idea.

12:51.103 --> 12:52.764
No, no, no. Don't think about it.

12:52.938 --> 12:55.998
Parenthood is like skydiving.
You gotta jump out of the old plane.

12:56.175 --> 12:58.439
And get sucked into the old propeller.

12:59.111 --> 13:01.102
A propeller of love.

13:01.614 --> 13:05.106
Hey, listen, why don't we go out
and talk about this over a couple of beers?

13:05.584 --> 13:09.486
Oh. Thanks. I really enjoy spending time
with you fellas, but I don't really drink.

13:09.655 --> 13:12.146
That's okay, neither do I.

13:13.859 --> 13:16.794
Well, okay, sure.
Let me just tell Judith I'm leaving.

13:16.962 --> 13:19.863
- No, that's okay. I'll tell her. We're leaving.
- Good.

13:20.032 --> 13:21.431
Let's go.

13:25.504 --> 13:29.304
My first wife and I tried to have kids,
but it just didn't happen.

13:29.808 --> 13:33.539
Then when she got sick and passed away,
I didn't think I'd ever have a family.

13:33.712 --> 13:36.875
- Oh, that's so sad.
- Yeah.

13:37.182 --> 13:39.514
Who was shooting blanks, you or her?

13:39.985 --> 13:44.479
Charlie, that doesn't matter. What matters
is that he's starting fresh with Judith.

13:45.090 --> 13:46.990
A live woman of proven fertility.

13:50.029 --> 13:53.157
What good does that do
if he's packing a starter's pistol?

13:53.632 --> 13:54.826
I'm fine.

13:55.000 --> 13:57.696
You hear that? He's fine.
Jake can have a little brother.

13:57.870 --> 14:01.738
- That would be a blessing from heaven.
- Oh, I don't know if I want more kids.

14:01.907 --> 14:03.636
Then wear a condom.

14:04.944 --> 14:07.037
Besides, Jake's used to being
an only child.

14:07.212 --> 14:10.670
If there was a new one,
he'd probably eat it by mistake.

14:12.351 --> 14:14.717
So, Herb, you haven't touched your beer.

14:14.887 --> 14:17.515
Oh, well, like I said,
I'm not much of a drinker.

14:17.890 --> 14:19.289
Then we need a drinking game.

14:20.292 --> 14:24.695
How about this? Each time Alan shoots me
a dirty look, we all take a drink.

14:26.131 --> 14:28.156
Oop. And here we go.

14:33.606 --> 14:35.540
You guys are great guys.

14:36.008 --> 14:37.270
I love you guys.

14:37.443 --> 14:39.934
You know why? Because you're great.

14:40.879 --> 14:44.440
You know, Herb, I wish more women
held their liquor the way you do.

14:44.617 --> 14:46.414
Thank you.

14:50.289 --> 14:52.280
I would like to propose a toast.

14:52.458 --> 14:54.187
- To Jake.
- Ah, Jake's great.

14:54.360 --> 14:57.261
- And to Judith.
- Absolutely. Judith's great too.

14:57.429 --> 14:59.624
And to your upcoming marriage.

14:59.898 --> 15:01.092
Ah, sure. What the hell.

15:06.538 --> 15:07.903
You know what I never had?

15:08.073 --> 15:10.064
A second beer?

15:11.443 --> 15:13.172
No, no, a bachelor party.

15:13.779 --> 15:15.610
Me neither. Thanks to my brother.

15:16.849 --> 15:18.316
Oop. Bottoms up.

15:19.952 --> 15:20.976
Mm.

15:21.153 --> 15:23.815
Hey, why don't we make this
your bachelor party?

15:23.989 --> 15:27.447
You know, one last big blowout
with your friends before you get married.

15:27.626 --> 15:30.618
- But my friends aren't here.
- What about us? We're your friends.

15:30.796 --> 15:33.060
We wish you well, right, Charlie?

15:33.232 --> 15:34.893
Well.

15:35.701 --> 15:37.328
Oh, come on, what do you say?

15:37.836 --> 15:39.804
I don't know. I mean...

15:39.972 --> 15:42.236
...if this is a bachelor party...

15:42.875 --> 15:45.366
...wouldn't there be a couple strippers?

15:47.613 --> 15:49.808
- Charlie?
- I'm on it.

16:03.095 --> 16:06.064
He's gonna make a great stepdad
for Jake.

16:06.231 --> 16:07.459
Yeah, whatever.

16:07.633 --> 16:10.796
And with the alimony I save,
I can go out to eat every night.

16:10.969 --> 16:13.961
In restaurants.
And I'm not talking early-bird special.

16:14.139 --> 16:18.235
I can eat when it's dark out
with people my own age.

16:23.482 --> 16:26.474
- Hey, does your cell phone have video?
- Yeah, why?

16:28.754 --> 16:30.278
Observe.

16:30.889 --> 16:32.288
What are you doing?

16:32.458 --> 16:35.188
Just in case he decides
to back out of the wedding.

16:35.360 --> 16:37.191
- That's blackmail.
- So?

16:37.362 --> 16:39.330
I like it.

16:40.432 --> 16:42.263
Hey, Herb.

16:44.937 --> 16:48.373
Attaboy. You dumb bastard.

16:52.277 --> 16:54.472
Uh-oh. It's Judith.

16:54.646 --> 16:56.671
Why is she calling me at this hour?

16:57.182 --> 16:58.740
Hello?

16:58.984 --> 17:01.179
Of course it's me.
Who were you expecting?

17:04.857 --> 17:07.553
Oh, my God, this is Herb's phone.

17:16.235 --> 17:19.033
Uh, Herb is in the bathroom.

17:19.204 --> 17:22.662
Yeah, we were just having a couple
of beers and getting to know each other.

17:23.442 --> 17:27.845
Well, with all due respect, Judith,
before we got married, I didn't drink either.

17:28.781 --> 17:32.410
Hey, hey. There is no call
for that kind of language.

17:34.019 --> 17:36.146
What? I'm sorry, I can't hear you.

17:37.089 --> 17:39.284
Yeah, I think this phone is...

17:39.458 --> 17:42.018
...running out of batteries.

17:42.194 --> 17:45.391
I said this phone
is running out of batteries.

17:46.965 --> 17:48.728
Goodbye, Judith.

17:50.869 --> 17:52.336
Think she bought it?

17:52.504 --> 17:53.528
If she did...

17:53.705 --> 17:55.536
...she's stupider than you.

17:58.911 --> 18:01.072
Excuse me, fellas.

18:01.246 --> 18:04.340
- Can either of you cash a check for me?
- Why?

18:04.516 --> 18:06.177
I'd like to tip the ladies.

18:06.351 --> 18:08.512
No, no, forget the tip.
We gotta get you home.

18:08.687 --> 18:10.951
Pssh. Why would I go home
when for a extra 300 bucks...

18:11.123 --> 18:13.489
...I can go all around the world?

18:14.326 --> 18:15.657
He's got a point, Alan.

18:16.862 --> 18:19.490
Herb, listen to me.
Your fiancée is worried about you.

18:20.232 --> 18:22.598
Oh. Right.

18:23.335 --> 18:27.135
Golly, she's gonna be pretty Po'd.

18:27.539 --> 18:31.339
- It's okay. She doesn't need to know.
- That's right. She doesn't need to know.

18:31.510 --> 18:33.637
Can I borrow $300?

18:35.614 --> 18:38.276
- What are you doing?
- Call it a wedding gift.

18:38.450 --> 18:41.214
- Are you crazy? I've gotta get him home.
- So take him home.

18:41.386 --> 18:42.944
What are you gonna do?

18:43.121 --> 18:45.214
I'm thinking,
maybe I'll go around the world.

18:45.390 --> 18:48.223
God knows I've racked up
enough frequent-flier miles.

18:50.863 --> 18:52.228
Herb?

18:53.665 --> 18:55.189
Herb?

18:55.968 --> 18:57.458
Herb?

18:58.670 --> 19:01.730
Charlie, you're gonna have to help me
take him home... Charlie?

19:10.449 --> 19:12.383
- You have a key?
- No, I don't have a key.

19:12.551 --> 19:14.985
- Maybe he's got a key.
- Wanna go through his pockets?

19:15.153 --> 19:16.211
Not particularly.

19:16.488 --> 19:19.184
Why don't we leave him on the porch,
ring the bell and run?

19:19.358 --> 19:22.384
He's not a bag of flaming dog poo.

19:22.928 --> 19:25.021
No, that was Judith's first husband.

19:26.598 --> 19:29.328
Oop. Dirty look. Where's my beer?

19:30.636 --> 19:33.799
All right, all right,
I'll go through his pockets.

19:35.374 --> 19:37.706
Ahh. Judith.

19:40.279 --> 19:41.746
What the hell is going on here?

19:51.757 --> 19:53.247
Well, that was close.

19:53.425 --> 19:55.290
No, it wasrt close.

19:55.460 --> 19:58.520
Close is when you get away with it.
That was nowhere near close.

19:58.697 --> 20:00.562
All right, all right, it doesn't matter.

20:00.732 --> 20:02.825
He had a good time,
he's gonna marry Judith...

20:03.001 --> 20:04.662
...and I'm off the hook for alimony.

20:04.836 --> 20:06.360
That's true.

20:09.007 --> 20:11.305
- Hey, Alan?
- Yeah?

20:11.476 --> 20:13.808
You did erase the video
from his cell phone, right?

20:15.314 --> 20:17.475
Oh, boy, it'd be really stupid if I didn't.

20:18.150 --> 20:19.708
Yes, it would.

20:24.256 --> 20:26.349
&lt;i>Hey, Herb. Attaboy.&lt;/i>

20:26.525 --> 20:28.493
&lt;i>You dumb bastard.&lt;/i>

20:32.898 --> 20:34.832
- Here you go.
- Thank you.

20:35.000 --> 20:36.865
Enjoy.

20:37.636 --> 20:41.402
Okay, so that's one root beer...

20:43.008 --> 20:45.602
...and one orange soda.
